3. The words of U.G. Krishnamurti quoted under teachers/ug-krishnamurti/
   carry his own release, printed in place of a copyright line in every
   book of his conversations:

   "My teaching, if that is the word you want to use, has no copyright.
   You are free to reproduce, distribute, interpret, misinterpret,
   distort, garble, do what you like, even claim authorship, without my
   consent or the permission of anybody."

   Wikisource and the Internet Archive treat the conversation books as
   public domain, released by the copyright holder, on the strength of it.

